    "id": "so-simba-mms-of-snow-depth-on-sea-ice-and-sea-ice-volume",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This merged multi-sensor record of snow depth is derived from the synergy of radar altimeters (CryoSat-2, Sentinel-3A/B) and laser altimetry (ICESat-2). The processing chain features: 1) retracking and along-track processing of CryoSat-2 and Sentinel-3A/B observations to retrieve Ku-band freeboard using the pysiral processing chain (https://github.com/pysiral/pysiral); 2) correction of ice-parcel positions using the DriftAware-SIAlt framework (https://github.com/robertricker/DriftAware-SIAlt) together with OSI SAF sea-ice drift products to ensure spatial and temporal co-location of radar and laser observations; and 3) retrieval of snow depth from the difference between ICESat-2 total freeboard and the merged drift-corrected Ku-band freeboard following a dual-altimetry approach. This dataset was generated by NORCE Norwegian Research Centre and funded by the ESA Polar Science Cluster project SO-SIMBA.",
